Build 032 (from the 031 freeze; the user chose recovery on):
- Before the GPU thread waits (for the CPU's next command, or polling a suspended channel's
  semaphore), it submits the work it recorded and did not submit (Scheduler::HasUnsubmittedWork,
  RasterizerInterface::SubmitRecordedWork; FlushCommands only counted draws). 031 froze with every
  channel waiting on a semaphore and the CPU on a syncpoint; only a frame capture's Finish()
  submitted the work (31 frames per capture). /data/eden-nx2/idle-flush-off.txt
  (EDEN_NX2_IDLE_FLUSH_OFF) restores the old behaviour.
- After 2 s without a command the GPU thread logs EDEN_GPU_STALL (waited ms, channels pending,
  syncpoint 1 guest/host) and recovers as a capture did: submit, then wait for the fences
  (EDEN_GPU_STALL_RECOVERED). /data/eden-nx2/stall-recovery-off.txt (EDEN_NX2_STALL_RECOVERY_OFF):
  log only. Recovery, not an explanation: a stall that recurs says the root cause is elsewhere.

